/// WebSocketHandler — protocol for Value handlers that serve one
/// WebSocket connection on the buccaneer backend.
///
/// Answer `HTTPResponse upgradeWebSocket: HandlerClass` from a block,
/// router or `HTTPHandler` actor and the adapter runs the connection
/// through the handler class. The handler is a Value and its own
/// state: `onOpen:request:` (sent to the class) answers the first
/// state, and each data callback answers the next state. Frames go
/// out through the `WebSocketHandle` (`sendText:`, `sendBinary:`,
/// `close:`), which the handler may keep in a field.
///
/// A handler that wants an actor forwards to one itself: create or
/// look up the actor in `onOpen:`, keep it in a field, and cast each
/// message to it. The actor pushes back by sending a message to the
/// connection process (`ws pid`), which arrives in `onInfo:`. The
/// actor never touches `ws`, which raises `#not_owner` outside the
/// connection process.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// sealed Value subclass: EchoHandler
///   class onOpen: ws :: WebSocketHandle request: req :: HTTPRequest -> EchoHandler =>
///     self new
///
///   onText: text :: String ws: ws :: WebSocketHandle -> EchoHandler =>
///     ws sendText: text
///     self
///
///   onClose: reason :: Object -> Object => nil
/// ```
Protocol define: WebSocketHandler
  /// Create the first handler state for a new connection. Sent to the
  /// handler class with a handle owned by the connection process and
  /// the upgrade's `HTTPRequest`.
  onOpen: ws :: WebSocketHandle request: req :: HTTPRequest -> Object
  /// A text frame. Answers the next handler state.
  onText: text :: String ws: ws :: WebSocketHandle -> Object
  /// A binary frame. Answers the next handler state.
  onBinary: data :: Binary ws: ws :: WebSocketHandle -> Object
  /// Any other message to the connection process (optional). Answers
  /// the next handler state.
  onInfo: message :: Object ws: ws :: WebSocketHandle -> Object
  /// The connection is ending (optional). Answers anything; the
  /// engine ignores it.
  onClose: reason :: Object -> Object
